---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n';

const strings = t('en');
---

<BaseLayout title={strings.meta.termsTitle} locale="en">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-neutral-900 mb-8">{strings.meta.termsTitle}</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none space-y-6 text-neutral-700">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> March 11, 2026</p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">1. Introduction and definitions</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms and Conditions of Use (hereinafter, the "<strong>Terms</strong>") govern access to
        and use of the PawMeet platform, consisting of the mobile application available for iOS and
        Android devices and the website <strong>pawmeet.io</strong> (hereinafter, collectively, the
        "<strong>Service</strong>" or the "<strong>Platform</strong>").
      </p>
      <p>
        The Service is operated by <strong>Cervera Studio</strong>,
        VAT IT04904730167 (hereinafter,
        "<strong>PawMeet</strong>", the "<strong>Owner</strong>", "<strong>we</strong>" or
        "<strong>our</strong>").
      </p>
      <p>For the purposes of these Terms:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li><strong>User</strong>: any natural person who accesses, registers for, or uses the Service in any way.</li>
        <li><strong>Account</strong>: the personal profile created by the User upon registration, required to access the Service features.</li>
        <li><strong>Dog Profile</strong>: the information card for a dog owned or cared for by the User, containing data such as name, breed, size, energy level, behavioral traits, and leash preferences.</li>
        <li><strong>Matching</strong>: the algorithmic process by which the Platform suggests other Users with potentially compatible dogs, based on predefined criteria.</li>
        <li><strong>User Content</strong> or <strong>UGC</strong> (User Generated Content): any content uploaded, published, or transmitted by the User through the Service, including text, photographs, videos, comments, messages, and profile information.</li>
        <li><strong>Group Event</strong>: a walk or activity organized by a User that other Users can join through the Platform.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">2. Acceptance of terms</h2>
      <p>
        Access to and use of the Service are subject to full and unconditional acceptance of these Terms,
        together with the <a href="/en/privacy" class="text-primary underline">Privacy Policy</a> and the
        <a href="/en/cookie" class="text-primary underline">Cookie Policy</a>, which form an integral part thereof.
      </p>
      <p>
        By creating an Account or using the Service in any way, the User declares to have read, understood,
        and accepted these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">3. Registration and account</h2>
      <p>
        To access the Service features, it is necessary to create an Account by providing: a valid email address,
        a password, a display name, and optionally a profile picture (avatar).
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">4. Age requirements</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is intended for Users who are at least 18 years old. Minors who are at least 14 years old
        may access the Service with verifiable parental consent, pursuant to applicable data protection regulations.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">5. Description of the service</h2>
      <p>
        PawMeet is a social platform for dog owners, designed to facilitate meeting people with behaviorally
        compatible dogs. The Service is currently offered completely free of charge.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">6. User obligations and conduct</h2>
      <p>
        The User agrees to use the Service lawfully, correctly, and in compliance with these Terms and applicable regulations.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">7. User Content (UGC)</h2>
      <p>
        The User is solely responsible for the Content they publish, upload, or transmit through the Service.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The Service, including its design, logo, name "PawMeet", source code, algorithms, architecture,
        user interfaces, original text, graphics, and databases, is the exclusive property of Cervera Studio.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, express or implied,
        to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">10. Geolocation and safety</h2>
      <p>
        The Service uses the User's geographic location to find nearby Users and calculate compatibility scores.
        Location sharing is optional and requires explicit consent.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">11. Account suspension and closure</h2>
      <p>
        PawMeet reserves the right to temporarily suspend or permanently close a User's Account in case of
        violation of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">12. Account and data deletion</h2>
      <p>
        The User may request deletion of their Account at any time through the app settings or by writing to
        <a href="mailto:info@cervera.studio" class="text-primary underline">info@cervera.studio</a>.
        A 30-day grace period applies before permanent deletion.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">13. Changes to the terms</h2>
      <p>
        PawMeet reserves the right to modify these Terms at any time. Substantial changes will be communicated
        with at least 30 days' notice.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">14. Applicable law and jurisdiction</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by Italian law. The Court of Milan has exclusive jurisdiction, subject to
        consumer protection regulations.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mt-8">15. Contact</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:info@cervera.studio" class="text-primary underline">info@cervera.studio</a></li>
        <li>Web: <a href="https://cervera.studio" class="text-primary underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cervera.studio</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-sm text-neutral-500 mt-12 border-t pt-6">
        These Terms and Conditions of Use are drafted in compliance with applicable Italian legislation,
        with particular reference to the Civil Code, Consumer Code (Legislative Decree 206/2005),
        Legislative Decree 70/2003 (e-commerce), Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR), and Legislative Decree
        196/2003 as amended by Legislative Decree 101/2018.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
